---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';import ArticleCard from '../../components/ArticleCard.astro';import {href} from '../../lib/paths';
---
<Base title="The engineering learning hub" description="Start a WaveLab experiment, find practical instrument guides, understand transmission-line concepts and troubleshoot result validity with clear assumptions." path="learn/"><div class="container"><header class="page-heading"><span class="eyebrow">Learn at your own depth</span><h1>From a first measurement<br/>to a physical explanation.</h1><p class="lede">Practical guides tell you what to do. Engineering concepts explain why. Experiments connect both.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button" href={href('learn/getting-started/')}>Start your first experiment →</a></div></header><div class="grid grid-2 section"><ArticleCard title="Practical user guides" description="Workbench connections, Manual and Auto, scope, Plot Studio, experiment templates and local projects." path="learn/guides/" label="Use the application"/><ArticleCard title="Engineering concepts" description="Understand characteristic impedance, propagation, reflection, matching, standing waves, attenuation and RLGC." path="learn/concepts/" label="Understand the physics"/><ArticleCard title="Five guided experiments" description="Follow a physical question through assumptions, equations, a supported setup and expected interpretation." path="experiments/" label="Connect theory and observation"/><ArticleCard title="FAQ & troubleshooting" description="Resolve real questions about the release, privacy, platforms and the meaning of common result states." path="learn/faq/" label="Find a precise answer"/></div><div class="callout"><h2>One important distinction</h2><p>The website teaches the model; it does not run a second simulator. Numerical examples are labelled independent analytical examples. Product screenshots come from the real application.</p></div></div></Base>
